<p>Yasser Abbas, the 64-year-old eldest son of Palestinian Authority President Mahmoud Abbas, won a seat on Fatah’s Central Committee after elections at the movement’s eighth general congress. The committee is Fatah’s top decision-making body, and preliminary results were released after voting at the end of the congress. Mahmoud Abbas, 90, was re-elected Fatah leader and will remain party chairman. Yasser Abbas is a businessman who spends much of his time in Canada.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/DWyi7cz9GXM2x-zljk7GvVGhqz15dHxINeomk0MLgFNK49503e6BFwfHjwelvEGqWlt7ymB-4aUM4FQ5ML3l3QiRrrEs6y1fR2qa7Zr9CEjhi2uOXtVjPxU3hstkxs5bjkLFOVV09ArRUOq367bY-Vb8sTmDLqrJWJ68KeV_sUIrTcPSZt-2H4Z-8xnudjG2xBoTG_uvWypbxpkf6G2Wy7JDylAe3_FaemQps9W7pJPjOGcN6xk-HSGcnctUEEjYvyT_7AQ7lkhvj-xMHlJu' alt='Yasser Abbas in a Reuters photo dated May 5, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Barghouti result: Marwan Barghouti, a senior Fatah figure, topped the preliminary Central Committee results and retained his seat.</li><li>Returning members: Hussein al-Sheikh, Mahmoud al-Aloul, Jibril Rajoub and Tawfiq al-Tirawi also kept seats on the committee.</li><li>New members: Newly elected members included Palestinian intelligence chief Majed Faraj and Zakaria Zubeidi, a former Al-Aqsa Martyrs Brigades figure from Jenin.</li><li>Congress format: The three-day congress was held simultaneously in Ramallah, Gaza City, Cairo and Beirut.</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/palestinian-leaders-son-wins-role-in-abbas-party-official-says/article70991196.ece'>Palestinian leader&#x27;s son wins role in Abbas&#x27; party, official says</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/5/17/son-of-palestinian-president-mahmoud-abbas-elected-to-top-fatah-body'>Son of Palestinian President Mahmoud Abbas elected to top Fatah body</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/05/palestinian-presidents-son-